# the Mach-O image writer: an executable from the image record of a link
#
# every address, file offset and size of a section comes from the layout
# record, and every byte of one from the relocated record, so the writer
# computes no address of the layout. it builds the Mach-O model the Mach-O
# writer turns into bytes. the header takes its cpu type and subtype from the
# architecture's code, the settled capability bits and the traits. a segment
# command maps each segment of the layout under the name of its format's
# segment, page zero below it reaching up to the image base, and
# __LINKEDIT after the last. LC_LOAD_DYLINKER names the system's loader,
# LC_BUILD_VERSION the platform of the environment, the oldest version of the
# target or else of the system, and the target's SDK, and LC_MAIN the entry.
# LC_LOAD_DYLIB, or LC_LOAD_WEAK_DYLIB where every import from it is weak,
# names each library the image loads with its install name and versions, its
# place among them the two-level ordinal its imports bind through, LC_RPATH
# each directory a runtime search path finds one of them in, and a
# main executable loads the libraries the system links every program
# against, as dyld refuses to run one that loads no libSystem. the
# link-edit data is the rebases and binds, the function starts, the data in
# code, the symbol table, the indirect symbol table and the names, each
# through its codec, and LC_UUID a hash of the image. the symbol table ends
# with an undefined symbol per import, by name, its library's ordinal in its
# description. a section holding a table of symbol pointers or stubs takes
# its type, and each of its slots an indirect symbol table entry in order,
# the import's symbol or the local marker. the writer writes each lazy
# pointer with its stub helper entry's address and emits the stub helper
# from its templates, each entry naming where its lazy binding lies. each
# thread-local variable descriptor binds the loader's accessor and holds the
# variable's offset in the thread-local template, its section and the
# section of the pointers to it taking their types, and the header states
# MH_HAS_TLV_DESCRIPTORS where the image holds one. where the link reserves a code signature at the end of the
# file, LC_CODE_SIGNATURE names an ad hoc superblob after every other
# link-edit blob, sized from the offset it starts at and the identifier the
# output's file name gives, whose code directory the Mach-O writer hashes
# once every byte before it is written.
#
# an address the image holds is rebased and a slot or pointer the loader
# binds is bound: through chained fixups from the version the system binds
# through them on, and through rebase, bind and lazy bind opcodes before it.
# a link that needs what the image cannot hold yet is refused, naming what it
# needs.

